# Wlroots 0.20.2 upstream requirements vs. what this system actually has:
#
#   dependency            upstream asks for   installed here      state
#   wayland-server        >= 1.24.0           1.26.0              OK
#   wayland-protocols     >= 1.47             1.49                OK
#   libdrm                >= 2.4.129          2.4.129             OK
#   xkbcommon             >= 1.8.0            1.8.0 (real)        OK
#   pixman-1              >= 0.46.0           0.46.4              OK
#   libinput              >= 1.19.0           1.31.3              OK
#
# The build system installs the real XKBcommon 1.8.0 (Recipes/XKBcommon/
# 1.8.0) and Pixman 0.46.4 (Recipes/Pantheon/Pixman/0.46.4) BEFORE Wlroots,
# so upstream's gates are satisfied.  wlroots-0.20.2-deps.patch additionally
# relaxes the gates and makes the two features that need the new libraries
# optional, so a failed dependency upgrade costs one niche feature instead
# of the whole build:
#   * pixman: PIXMAN_a16b16g16r16 (16 bits per component, used for
#     DRM_FORMAT_ABGR16161616) only exists from pixman 0.46.0 on.  The patch
#     guards that one format entry with the pixman version.
#   * xkbcommon: XKB_LED_NAME_COMPOSE and XKB_LED_NAME_KANA only exist from
#     xkbcommon 1.8.0 on.  The patch spells those two stable LED names out.
#
# Other optional-but-present dependencies that are enabled automatically:
# libdisplay-info 0.3.0, libliftoff 0.5.0, libseat 0.6.4, libudev 243,
# hwdata 0.410, xcb 1.13.1 + xcb-* (X11 backend), xwayland 24.1.2,
# gbm 25.3.6, glesv2 3.2, egl 1.5, vulkan 1.4.357, lcms2 2.9.
#
# The build system's step_sync loop copies the wayland-core recipes into
# /Data/Compile/Recipes; step_sway compiles "Wlroots 0.20.2".
